---
import BlogPostLayout from "../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro";
import DetailInteractions from "../../components/DetailInteractions.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/paths";
---

<BlogPostLayout
	title="受持。"
	description="真正懂，不是会复述，而是能在事上用出来。"
	keywords="金刚经,学习方法,重复学习,理解,受持,读书感悟"
	image="/assets/cover/share-jingangjing-learning-fourth-read.jpg"
	canonicalPath="/notes/jingangjing-learning-fourth-read/"
>
	<main class="reading-note">
		<section class="note-hero">
			<img src={withBase('/assets/cover/cover-jingangjing-learning-fourth-read.webp')} alt="书本在灯光下逐步展开，象征学习从熟悉走向理解" />
		</section>

		<article class="note-content">
			<a class="note-back" href={withBase('/')} aria-label="返回首页">
				<span>←</span>
				返回首页
			</a>
			<div class="note-meta">READING NOTE · 2026.06.19</div>
			<h1 class="font-huiwen">受持。</h1>
			<p class="lead">真正懂，不是会复述，而是能在事上用出来。</p>

			<p>《金刚经》里常说“受持”。受，是把一句话真正接进心里；持，是在日常里保持它、验证它、用它修正自己。读过、背过、讲得出来，都还只是外层。真正的受持，是这句话在你遇事时能起作用。</p>
			<p>比如“应无所住而生其心”。如果只会解释，它还是知识；如果在被误解、被甩脸色、被结果牵动时，能提醒自己：我该做的做，但不把心交给对方反应，这才开始受持。</p>
			<p>这也对应学习。第一遍是识别，第二遍是熟悉，第三遍发现漏洞，第四遍才开始把知识拆开、重组、应用。佛法也是这样。经文没有变，是读的人变了；不是突然开窍，而是重复之后，某句话终于从“内容”变成“工具”。</p>
			<p>所以不要急着追求“我懂了”。更有效的问题是：这句话今天能不能少让我被一个相带走？能不能让我少一次内耗？能不能让我多一点清明？</p>

			<section class="note-reminder">
				<h2>今日小提醒</h2>
				<p>今天选一句你记得的《金刚经》话，不解释它，只在一个具体场景里用一次。</p>
			</section>
		</article>
		<DetailInteractions
			articleSelector=".note-content"
			storageKey="jingangjing-learning-fourth-read-comments"
		/>
	</main>
</BlogPostLayout>

<style lang="scss">
	:global(.train-1) {
		display: none !important;
	}

	.reading-note {
		width: 100%;
		margin: 0 auto 88px;
	}

	.note-hero {
		width: min(1120px, calc(100vw - 48px));
		margin: 56px auto 72px;

		img {
			display: block;
			width: 100%;
			height: auto;
		}
	}

	.note-back {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 7px;
		margin: 0 0 22px;
		padding: 0;
		border: 0;
		background: transparent;
		color: var(--color-400);
		font-size: 0.86rem;
		line-height: 1;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: color 0.22s ease, transform 0.22s ease;

		span {
			font-size: 0.95rem;
			transform: translateY(-1px);
		}

		&:hover {
			transform: translateX(-3px);
			color: #8b6a2b;
			text-decoration: none;
		}
	}

	.note-content {
		max-width: 760px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 0 24px;

		h1 {
			margin: 12px 0 32px;
			font-family: 'Huiwen-mincho', serif !important;
			font-size: clamp(2.35rem, 4vw, 3.7rem);
			font-weight: 400;
			line-height: 1.22;
			color: var(--color-100);
			letter-spacing: 0;
			text-align: left;
		}

		p {
			margin: 0 0 1.35em;
			color: var(--color-200);
			font-size: 1.08rem;
			line-height: 2.05;
		}

		.lead {
			color: #8b6a2b;
			font-family: 'Huiwen-mincho', var(--font-body);
			font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.6vw, 1.9rem);
			line-height: 1.62;
			margin-bottom: 1.45em;
		}
	}

	.note-meta {
		color: #9b7a35;
		font-family: var(--font-type);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	}

	.note-reminder {
		margin-top: 44px;
		padding: 22px 0 0 22px;
		border-top: 1px solid rgba(184, 138, 55, 0.22);
		border-left: 3px solid rgba(184, 138, 55, 0.7);

		h2 {
			margin-bottom: 12px;
			color: var(--color-100);
			font-size: 1.28rem;
		}

		p {
			margin-bottom: 0;
		}
	}

	@media(max-width: 767px) {
		.note-hero {
			width: calc(100vw - 32px);
			margin-top: 34px;
			margin-bottom: 48px;
		}

		.note-content {
			padding: 0 22px;

			h1 {
				font-size: 2.15rem;
				line-height: 1.24;
			}

			p {
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.95;
			}
		}
	}
</style>
